    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nPick\n\n### Description\n\nUsing...\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.pick').setup({\r\n  window = {\r\n    config = {\r\n      border = {\r\n        { 'x', 'Red' }, { 'x', 'Red' }, { 'x', 'Red' },\r\n        ' ',\r\n        { 'x', 'Red' }, { 'x', 'Red' }, { 'x', 'Red' },\r\n        ' '\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\n... causes Pick to show no results and immediately exit on any key press.\n\n### Neovim version\n\nGit\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. Setup mini.pick as above\r\n3. `:lua require('mini.pick').builtin.files()`\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n_No response_\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nSee above",
